    "description": "Pressed Glass Insulator Lot - 12 Pieces\nWhitall Tatum, Armstrong, and Pyrex\nAqua, Clear, and Smoky, Vintage 1920s-1950s\nThis collection features twelve vintage glass telephone and telegraph insulators from prominent American manufacturers. These pieces represent a significant era in telecommunications history, showcasing various industrial glass formulas including standard aqua, clear, and heat-resistant Pyrex borosilicate glass. Matching sets and mixed lots from these manufacturers are highly collectible for their industrial aesthetic and historical utility.\nPieces Included:\nWhitall Tatum Co. No. 1, Aqua Glass - characteristic greenish-blue tint, molded manufacturer marks on base\nPyrex Clear Glass Insulator - high-clarity borosilicate glass, marked \"Pyrex Reg. U.S. Pat. Off.\"\nArmstrong \"W\" in Triangle Mark, Aqua Glass - produced after Armstrong's 1938 acquisition of Whitall Tatum\nArmstrong T.W. Smoky/Clear Glass - industrial clear glass with age-appropriate tinting and molded date codes\nAdditional assorted aqua and clear pressed glass insulators to complete the 12-piece set\nCondition:\nThe lot is in good vintage condition consistent with outdoor industrial use. Several pieces show characteristic rust staining near the thread interior and top grooves from contact with metal mounting brackets. No significant structural cracks observed. Minor fleabites and surface scratches may be present on rims or skirts. All molded lettering remains legible.",
